      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This is the piyyut, “Aamir Otekha Selah” by Elazar ben Qallir for Sukkot, as translated into rhyming English verse by Alice Montefiore Lucas, first published as “Hymn for Tabernacles” in her anthology of versified translations <tei:hi rend="italic">Songs of Zion by Hebrew Singers of Mediæval Times</tei:hi> (1894). (The translation was reprinted in her <tei:hi rend="italic">The Jewish Year</tei:hi> (1898) under the title, “Palm and Myrtles.”) Her translation was later set opposite Qallir’s Hebrew text in <tei:hi rend="italic">Maḥzor Avodat Ohel Moed: Avodat Ḥag haSukkot</tei:hi> (ed. Arthur Davis &amp; Herbert Adler, 1908).</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_66395_notes"/>
